{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California residential security deposit cap and return rules","requirement":"A landlord may not demand or receive security above one month's rent (two months for qualifying small natural-person landlords), and must itemize and return any remaining security within 21 days after the tenant vacates.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 2 months' rent for qualifying small landlords","coverage_conditions":"Security for a rental agreement for residential property used as the dwelling of the tenant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Residential property used as the tenant's dwelling"},"exemptions":"Advance payment of six months' rent or more if the lease term is six months or longer; tenant-requested alterations for a fee; security collected before July 1, 2024; the two-month small-landlord amount does not apply to service members.","penalty":"A landlord that in bad faith fails to comply with the itemization and return duties may not claim any amount of the security; a successor in interest is jointly and severally liable for transfer violations.","effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"Except as provided in paragraph (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant-processing fees counted as capped security","requirement":"A payment, fee, deposit or charge imposed at the beginning of a tenancy to reimburse the landlord for costs of processing a new tenant counts as 'security' and is subject to the one-month security cap, except charges under Civil Code § 1950.6.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential property used as the tenant's dwelling; charges imposed at the beginning of the tenancy for processing a new tenant or as advance rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancy"},"exemptions":"Charges provided for in Section 1950.6.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"As used in this section, “security” means any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, including, but not limited to, any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, except as provided in Section 1950.6, that is imposed at the beginning of the tenancy to be used to reimburse the landlord for costs associated with processing a new tenant","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
